  "raw_text": "250\n\nTatumra\n \n(\nsee/ver:\n \nTumaia\n)\n \n(adj\n,\nn\n-\nagent\n/s\n-\nagente\n)\n \n–\n \nenvious\n,\n \njealous,\n \nenvy, jealousy,\n \nenv\nious person\n, jealous person\n \n/\n\ne\nnvidioso, celoso, envidi\no\n, celos, persona envidios\no\n, persona celos\no\n\nTatuskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto instigate, to coax, to persuade, to induce, to entice, to urge, to encourage\n \n/ instigar, persuadir,\ninducir, incitar, instar, alentar\n\nTatwa\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \npointy, having a sharp point\n \n/ puntiagudo, que tiene una punta afilada\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb32\n):\n \nJael ... tint watla dusa tatwa kum wal lal ra saban, bara witin pruan\n \n–\n \nJael ... stabbed (him) in the head with a pointy\ntent peg, and he died\n \n/ Jael ... lo apuñaló en la cabeza con una clavija puntiaguda y murió)\n\nAyan dusa tatwa\n \n(\nmwb-01/19\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ngoad\n \n/ aguijón\n\nTaua\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nTawa\n\nTaua taua\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nTawa tawa\n\nTauaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nTawaia\n\nTaukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto roam, to travel, to walk about, to walk\n \n/ vagar, viajar, caminar, andar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n\nWapaia\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nlfb4\n):\n \nAbel pain tauki kan\n \n–\n \nAbel was walking in a good way\n \n/ Abel caminaba en una buena forma)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nmwb-04/20\n):\n \nPâna saura nani wal upla taukisa taim pât nani takisa\n \n–\n \nWhen we walk with bad associates, trouble happens\n \n/\nCuando caminamos con malos asociados, ocurren problemas)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nwqu-07/20\n):\n \nTânka kasak ba kat taukaia dukiara yawan dîa daukaia sa?\n \n–\n \nWhat must we do in order to walk according to\nthe truth?\n \n/ ¿Qué debemos hacer para caminar de acuerdo con la verdad?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-08/20\n):\n \nBawan lâka bara tânkira ni Gâd lamara tauki kap\n \n–\n \nBe walking close to God with humility and modesty\n \n/\nAndemos junto a Dios con humildad y modestia)\n\nBrih taukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \ncarrying/taking while travelling\n \n/ llevar mientras viaja\n\nPirwi taukaia\n \n(\ndb-Hibru Nani 11:38\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto wander\n \n/ vagar\n\nSmalki taukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto go preaching/teaching\n \n/ ir a predicar/enseñar\n\nTataukra\n \n(adj,n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nsomeone who roams ??\n\nSmalki tataukra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncongregation publisher\n \n/ publicador de congregación\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n07/19\n):\n \nDîa muni\n \nsmalki\n \ntataukra nani sut ba hilp munisa upla kum kangrigisan ra dimbia dukiara?\n \n–\n\nWhy do all the publishers help a person enter into the congregation?\n \n/ ¿Por qué todos los\n \npublicadores\n \nayudan a\n\nuna persona a ingresar a la congregación?\n)\n\nSmalki Tataukra Warkka Waukataya\n \n–\n \nPublisher Record Card\n \n/ tarejta\n \nde R\negistro de publicador\n\nde la congregaci\nó\nn\n\nSmalki tataukra kau aihtabi takras\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nunbaptized publisher\n \n/ publicador no bautizado\n\nTaun\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nTawan\n \n–\n \ntown, village, city\n, nation\n \n/ pueblo, ciudad,\n \nnación\n\nTaun tnaya kutbanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nTaun naya kutbanka\n,\n \nTaun snaya kutbanka\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncity wall\n \n/\n \nmuralla\n \nde la cuidad\n\nTâura\n \n(Taura)\n \n–\n \nat the beginning, at the front, above all, ahead\n \n/ al principio, al frente, sobre todo, adelante\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Blasi Sturka 1:1\n):\n \nKau diara wala nani sut paskras kan ba tâura,...\n \n–\n \nIn the beginning (when) things were still not\ncreated,...\n \n/ Al principio (cuando) las cosas aún no se creaban,...)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-14\n):\n \nAisankam tâura, tânka tara nani ba wiaia sip sma\n \n–\n \nAt the beginning of your talk, you can state the main points\n \n/ Al\ncomienzo de su discurso, puede decir los puntos principales)\n\nAi tâura\n \n–\n \nahead of him or her, in front of him or her\n \n/ delante de él o ella\n\nPas tâura\n \n–\n \nfirst above all, first at the beginning, first place\n \n/ primero sobre todo, primero al principio, primer\nlugar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-11/18\n):\n \nMan ba dîa daukram Gâd kingka lâka rayakam ra pas tâura mangkaia dukiara?\n \n–\n \nWhat have you done\nin order to\n \nplace God’s kingdom first above all in your life?\n \n/ ¿Qué has hecho para colocar el reino de Dios primero sobre\ntodo en tu vida?)\n\nTâira\n \n–\n \nahead of me, in front of me\n \n/ delante de mí\n\nTamra\n \n–\n \nahead of you, in front of you\n \n/ delante de ti\n\nTâura impakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto move ahead, to move forward\n \n/ avanzar\n\nTâura mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto put/place ahead, to put/place at the front or beginning\n \n/ poner/colocar adelante, poner\n/colocar al frente o al comienzo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-19/04\n):\n \nNahki upla kum sip sa smalkaia warkka ba ai rayaka ra tâura mangkaia?\n \n–\n \nHow is a person able to put\nthe preaching work at the front in their life?\n \n/ ¿Cómo puede una persona poner la predicación al frente de su vida?)\n\nTâura smasmalkra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \n(regular)\n \npioneer (of Jehovah’s Witnesses)\n \n/ precursor (regular) (de los testigos de\nJehová)",
